{% set local_problem %}
<p>Rural Toney properties have serious tree coverage — and that means serious gutter debris. Pine needles accumulate year-round. Oak and maple leaves drop by the truckload in fall. And without regular cleaning, that debris compacts into gutter-clogging sludge.</p>

<p>Clogged gutters don't just overflow — they damage your home. Water cascades over the gutter edge, erodes landscaping, and pools against your foundation. On Toney's clay soil, that water doesn't drain away — it sits there, eventually finding its way into crawlspaces and basements.</p>

<p>Many Toney homeowners try to clean gutters themselves, but it's dangerous, time-consuming work — especially on larger rural properties with tall rooflines. Professional cleaning is faster, safer, and more thorough.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our cleaning service is comprehensive. We remove all debris by hand — leaves, pine needles, shingle grit, and the composted gunk that builds up over time. We don't just blow debris around or push it toward downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear. Downspout clogs are common and often missed by DIY cleaning. A clogged downspout makes clean gutters useless.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire system for problems: loose hangers, small leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage. We'll report what we find so you can address issues before they become expensive repairs.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters on Toney properties for over 20 years. We understand rural properties — longer driveways, taller homes, heavier tree coverage. Our crews come prepared with the right equipment and don't rush through the job.</p>

<p>When we're done, we clean up completely. No debris left in your yard, no mess on your driveway. Your property will look better than when we arrived.</p>
{% endset %}
